('127.226.d.6.A',3,'A student secures a tripod and tapes down cables before a shoot. This is following:','["price rules", "safety rules", "style rules", "spelling rules"]'::jsonb,1,'Safety measures prevent accidents.','original'),
('127.226.d.6.A',4,'Which action reflects workplace safety in a studio?','["Leaving cords across walkways", "Plugging many devices into one outlet", "Never overloading electrical outlets", "Ignoring sparks"]'::jsonb,2,'Overloaded outlets cause fires.','original'),
('127.226.d.6.B',3,'A student notices a heavy light on an unstable stand. The best action is to:','["use it anyway", "leave it", "push it aside", "report it and fix or replace the stand"]'::jsonb,3,'Resolve concerns before someone is hurt.','original'),
('127.226.d.6.B',4,'Loud audio at high volume for hours can damage hearing. Which step helps?','["Lower the volume and take listening breaks", "Remove ear protection", "Raise the volume", "Skip breaks"]'::jsonb,0,'Safe levels protect hearing.','original'),
('127.226.d.6.C',3,'If a smoke alarm goes off in the studio, staff should:','["hide", "exit by the posted route", "keep recording", "turn off the alarm and stay"]'::jsonb,1,'Follow the emergency plan.','original'),
('127.226.d.6.C',4,'Where should a fire extinguisher be located in a studio?','["Behind equipment", "Locked in a closet", "In a clear, visible spot near an exit", "Under a table"]'::jsonb,2,'Emergency tools must be easy to reach.','original'),
('127.226.d.7.A',3,'A producer sets goals, assigns tasks, and motivates the crew. She is showing:','["avoidance", "confusion", "laziness", "leadership"]'::jsonb,3,'Leaders guide groups toward goals.','original'),
('127.226.d.7.A',4,'When a deadline is at risk, a good leader will:','["analyze the problem and reassign tasks", "stop the project", "blame an intern", "ignore it"]'::jsonb,0,'Leaders respond to obstacles.','original'),
